  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v5.8.25 - on SpawnDev.ILGPU 5.4.42. Tensors stay on the GPU (rule 4, for SpawnGen's device-resident IMAGE / LATENT): DeviceFrames on the Wan, LTX and LTX-2 requests returns the video as a device buffer in ComfyUI's IMAGE layout ([F, H, W, 3] in 0..1, the caller owns it; tiled Wan blends on the device); with it the Wan denoising loop keeps the latent, guidance, sampler step and image-to-video frame on the device, and every decoder reads the device latent. Device VAE paths: decode from a device latent (Wan, LTX, LTX-2), device encode (Wan 2.2 / 2.1, LTX, LTX-2), ComfyUI IMAGE overloads on SdVae and SdTaesd, ImageTensorKernels (IMAGE to channel-first and back), LtxPipeline.DenoiseDeviceAsync, LTX / LTX-2 UpsampleDeviceAsync (AdaIN on the device). FLUX.1, Z-Image, Qwen-Image and FLUX.2 transformers can write their output into the caller's buffer. Speed: the Stable Diffusion VAE's 3x3 convolutions about 2x faster (a VAE loaded from an fp32 file ran each one twice, once more for the weights' low halves; now one pass, and the gather index math is hoisted): WebGPU 278 -> 134 ms for the decoder's conv shapes on an RTX 4070. Device and host paths match bit for bit except the Wan device loop (float32 sampler; within the host's own rounding spread) and the upsamplers' device AdaIN (8.5e-8).",
